<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/infographic-sme-transformation-order.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<div class="n3l-sme-transformation-order">
<figure class="fig">

  <header class="mast">
    <span class="eyebrow brand-eyebrow">NEXT3LABS &mdash; Singapore SME digital transformation</span>
    <div class="title">The stage order that <span class="hi">actually works</span>.</div>
    <p class="sub">Most transformations do not fail on the technology. They fail on <strong>sequence</strong> &mdash; automation bolted onto a process nobody wrote down.</p>
    <div class="mast-rule"></div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrong">
    <span class="eyebrow wrong-label">The order that fails</span>
    <p class="wrong-line">Buy the platform <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> point it at the existing process <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> <b>the mess just runs faster</b></p>
  </div>

  <div class="steps-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">The order that holds &mdash; five stages, run in this sequence</span>
    <span class="legend"><i class="mark mini" aria-hidden="true"><b>&rarr;</b></i> finish this, then the next</span>
  </div>

  <ol class="steps">

    <li class="step">
      <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <div class="body">
        <h3>Write down the process as it actually runs</h3>
        <p>Not as the org chart says it runs. No AI in this stage &mdash; and it is the one most often skipped.</p>
      </div>
      <i class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><b>&rarr;</b></i>
    </li>

    <li class="step">
      <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <div class="body">
        <h3>Decide what &ldquo;correct&rdquo; means before automating</h3>
        <p>No reconciliation, no external check, no number to compare against &mdash; then there is nothing to verify against yet.</p>
      </div>
      <i class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><b>&rarr;</b></i>
    </li>

    <li class="step">
      <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div class="body">
        <h3>Automate the bounded, well-specified slice</h3>
        <p>One slice with a clear boundary and a checkable output. Ambiguous judgement calls stay with a person.</p>
      </div>
      <i class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><b>&rarr;</b></i>
    </li>

    <li class="step step--gate">
      <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
      <div class="body">
        <h3>Verify against something the tool does not control</h3>
        <p><b class="gate-em">A dashboard the automation fills in is not a check.</b> A bank statement, a government portal, a customer confirmation is.</p>
      </div>
      <i class="mark mark--gate" aria-hidden="true"><b>&rarr;</b></i>
    </li>

    <li class="step step--last">
      <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
      <div class="body">
        <h3>Only then widen scope</h3>
        <p>Extend the same pattern to the next slice. Small checked expansions, not a big-bang go-live.</p>
      </div>
      <i class="mark mark--end" aria-hidden="true"><b>&#10003;</b></i>
    </li>

  </ol>

  <section class="rules">
    <span class="eyebrow rules-label">Where SMEs lose it</span>
    <ul class="rule-list">
      <li class="rule-item">No change-management function, so stage 1 gets skipped by default &mdash; not by decision.</li>
      <li class="rule-item">The owner knows the process in their head, so writing it down feels like busywork.</li>
      <li class="rule-item">Skip stage 4 and the failure is not &ldquo;it broke&rdquo; &mdash; it is quietly wrong for six weeks.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <figcaption class="foot">
    <span class="mark-word">NEXT3LABS</span>
    <span>Process map first, demo second &middot; next3labs.com</span>
  </figcaption>

</figure>
</div>
